  "review": "Native originals only. First source checks a caller-owned temporary across invocation; second suspends a reference iterator while a callee appends to its global array. A passed array survives global unset. Returned local singleton references separate on COW (17), while an additional global reference owner preserves sharing (777). Callee division failure retains outputBA and native call stack. These are future frame ownership/diagnostic obligations, not accepted source execution.",
